1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,504
India sells medicines to around two hundred countries.

2
00:00:03,504 --> 00:00:06,837
That's why you hear it called the pharmacy of the world.

3
00:00:06,837 --> 00:00:11,583
But open one antibiotic capsule and look at the white powder inside.

4
00:00:11,583 --> 00:00:16,947
That's the actual medicine... and there's a fair chance its journey began in China.

5
00:00:16,947 --> 00:00:20,221
The rest of the capsule is just there to carry it to you.

6
00:00:20,221 --> 00:00:22,122
Now think back to the Corona days.

7
00:00:22,122 --> 00:00:23,140
You remember them.

8
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:26,204
Not the lockdown yet — this is three weeks before it.

9
00:00:26,204 --> 00:00:28,528
The third of March, twenty twenty.

10
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:33,082
In China, the city of Wuhan has been locked down for almost six weeks.

11
00:00:33,082 --> 00:00:36,487
Here in India, there are only a handful of cases so far.

12
00:00:36,487 --> 00:00:37,315
Delhi.

13
00:00:37,315 --> 00:00:42,927
A two-page government order goes out, and if you run a medicine company, your phone starts ringing.

14
00:00:42,927 --> 00:00:48,768
Thirteen medicine ingredients, and the medicines made from them, can't leave India without a licence.

15
00:00:48,768 --> 00:00:50,786
Paracetamol is one of them.

16
00:00:50,786 --> 00:00:51,489
Wait.

17
00:00:51,489 --> 00:00:52,369
India?

18
00:00:52,369 --> 00:00:55,793
The pharmacy of the world... locking its own doors?

19
00:00:55,793 --> 00:00:56,559
Yes.

20
00:00:56,559 --> 00:00:58,499
And the reason was Corona.

21
00:00:58,499 --> 00:01:03,661
Wuhan sits in a Chinese province called Hubei... and the whole province was shut down.

22
00:01:03,661 --> 00:01:08,840
Reports at the time said many of the ingredients on that list came from that one place.

23
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:11,552
So here's the question I want to answer for you today.

24
00:01:11,552 --> 00:01:16,933
If India makes medicine for the world... who makes the powder inside India's medicine?

25
00:01:16,933 --> 00:01:20,692
And before you worry — this isn't about the quality of your medicines.

26
00:01:20,692 --> 00:01:23,769
It's about who controls the supply.

27
00:01:23,769 --> 00:01:24,873
Stay with me.

28
00:01:24,873 --> 00:01:30,388
Around minute eight, I'll take you to a fight India is in right now — in Andhra Pradesh.

29
00:01:30,388 --> 00:01:33,872
And I'll give you the date that could decide how it ends.

30
00:01:33,872 --> 00:01:36,186
First, let's give India its due.

31
00:01:36,186 --> 00:01:38,395
Because that pharmacy of the world title?

32
00:01:38,395 --> 00:01:40,051
India earned it.

33
00:01:40,051 --> 00:01:41,842
Think back to two thousand one.

34
00:01:41,842 --> 00:01:44,534
H.I.V. is killing millions in Africa.

35
00:01:44,534 --> 00:01:50,761
The medicines exist... but the Western price is around ten thousand dollars a year for one patient.

36
00:01:50,761 --> 00:01:57,611
Then an Indian company, Cipla, stands up and offers the same three-drug mix for about a dollar a day.

37
00:01:57,611 --> 00:01:58,783
One dollar.

38
00:01:58,783 --> 00:02:02,692
That one offer helped change how the world priced these medicines.

39
00:02:02,692 --> 00:02:09,008
And today, you'll find India sells medicines abroad worth more than two and a half lakh crore rupees a year.

40
00:02:09,008 --> 00:02:11,199
So where's the missing piece?

41
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:12,297
Here's the catch.

42
00:02:12,297 --> 00:02:14,389
Every tablet has two parts.

43
00:02:14,389 --> 00:02:17,039
There's the powder that actually makes you better.

44
00:02:17,039 --> 00:02:21,158
The industry calls it the A.P.I. — and no, not the computer kind.

45
00:02:21,158 --> 00:02:22,713
Let's just call it the powder.

46
00:02:22,713 --> 00:02:28,633
And then there's everything around it... the rest of the tablet, the coating, the strip, the box.

47
00:02:28,633 --> 00:02:30,297
And you should be proud of this.

48
00:02:30,297 --> 00:02:33,424
Indian companies are world class at that last part.

49
00:02:33,424 --> 00:02:38,623
Mixing, pressing, packing, and passing the toughest inspections on the planet.

50
00:02:38,623 --> 00:02:40,160
But the powder you swallow?

51
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,879
A lot of it is made somewhere else first.

52
00:02:42,879 --> 00:02:49,662
In twenty twenty-five, India bought these powders from other countries worth around sixty-five thousand crore rupees.

53
00:02:49,662 --> 00:02:51,897
And the biggest seller, by far...

54
00:02:51,897 --> 00:02:53,233
China.

55
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:56,515
And if you look at antibiotics, it gets worse.

56
00:02:56,515 --> 00:03:07,617
Niti Aayog — that's the government's own think tank — says out of every hundred rupees India spent on imported antibiotic powder... about eighty-six went to China.

57
00:03:07,617 --> 00:03:10,064
Even your fever tablet has a China link.

58
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:12,875
Indian factories do make paracetamol powder.

59
00:03:12,875 --> 00:03:14,809
But the raw chemical it's made from?

60
00:03:14,809 --> 00:03:19,145
Industry reports say a big share of that still comes from China.

61
00:03:19,145 --> 00:03:22,285
So you might be thinking — has it always been like this?

62
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:24,534
Did India ever make its own powder?

63
00:03:24,534 --> 00:03:25,406
It did.

64
00:03:25,406 --> 00:03:29,398
And this part of the story, most people have never heard.

65
00:03:29,398 --> 00:03:31,195
Pimpri, near Pune.

66
00:03:31,195 --> 00:03:32,641
Nineteen fifty-four.

67
00:03:32,641 --> 00:03:38,641
India has been free for less than seven years, and it's building a factory to make its own penicillin.

68
00:03:38,641 --> 00:03:41,346
Penicillin was the miracle drug of that time.

69
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:44,486
Back then, a small cut on your hand could kill you.

70
00:03:44,486 --> 00:03:48,032
With penicillin, it became a few days of medicine for you.

71
00:03:48,032 --> 00:03:51,824
The government sets up a company called Hindustan Antibiotics.

72
00:03:51,824 --> 00:03:56,873
By nineteen fifty-six, Indian penicillin is coming out of Indian tanks.

73
00:03:56,873 --> 00:03:58,125
Just think about it.

74
00:03:58,125 --> 00:04:00,144
Picture your grandparents' India.

75
00:04:00,144 --> 00:04:06,779
A young, poor country, growing one of the most important medicines on earth... in its own factory.

76
00:04:06,779 --> 00:04:12,789
Soon, others join in — big names you may know, like Alembic, Sarabhai and Ranbaxy.

77
00:04:12,789 --> 00:04:15,911
India is making its own antibiotics.

78
00:04:15,911 --> 00:04:19,291
But to see what happened next, you need to know one thing.

79
00:04:19,291 --> 00:04:22,201
How do you actually make penicillin?

80
00:04:22,201 --> 00:04:27,716
Many medicines, like paracetamol, are cooked from chemicals, step by step.

81
00:04:27,716 --> 00:04:29,369
Penicillin is different.

82
00:04:29,369 --> 00:04:31,205
Penicillin is grown.

83
00:04:31,205 --> 00:04:35,925
You take a special mould... a cousin of the green patches you've seen on old bread.

84
00:04:35,925 --> 00:04:40,177
You put it in a giant steel tank, and you feed it sugar and air.

85
00:04:40,177 --> 00:04:43,356
For about a week, the tank runs day and night.

86
00:04:43,356 --> 00:04:47,580
The mould eats, grows, and gives out penicillin into the liquid.

87
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:52,028
And if even one stray germ gets in, you can lose the whole batch.

88
00:04:52,028 --> 00:04:54,809
Then you take the penicillin out and clean it.

89
00:04:54,809 --> 00:04:57,755
This first powder is called penicillin G.

90
00:04:57,755 --> 00:05:00,821
Next, it's turned into a smaller base powder.

91
00:05:00,821 --> 00:05:05,065
Factories call it six A.P.A., but let's just call it the base.

92
00:05:05,065 --> 00:05:10,832
From that base, factories make amoxicillin — the antibiotic in so many strips at home.

93
00:05:10,832 --> 00:05:13,054
Now here's the secret of this business.

94
00:05:13,054 --> 00:05:15,649
A bigger tank makes the powder cheaper.

95
00:05:15,649 --> 00:05:16,953
Much cheaper.

96
00:05:16,953 --> 00:05:17,756
Why?

97
00:05:17,756 --> 00:05:23,988
The tank must stay perfectly clean, cool, and full of air, every hour of every day.

98
00:05:23,988 --> 00:05:27,396
That takes a lot of power, water and steam.

99
00:05:27,396 --> 00:05:28,748
Think of a flour mill.

100
00:05:28,748 --> 00:05:32,505
A big chakki grinds each kilo cheaper than a small one.

101
00:05:32,505 --> 00:05:36,846
Double your tank, and your costs don't double... but your output does.

102
00:05:36,846 --> 00:05:38,766
So you can guess who wins.

103
00:05:38,766 --> 00:05:42,120
The country with the biggest tanks and the cheapest power.

104
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:45,324
And that's exactly where India's story turns.

105
00:05:45,324 --> 00:05:47,405
Now, here's what we got wrong.

106
00:05:47,405 --> 00:05:53,883
For years, India's government allowed only a few companies to make penicillin, and only in small amounts.

107
00:05:53,883 --> 00:05:57,491
So our plants stayed too small to be cheap.

108
00:05:57,491 --> 00:06:02,587
Meanwhile, in the nineteen nineties, China went all in on medicine ingredients.

109
00:06:02,587 --> 00:06:07,892
It built huge plants, in huge drug parks, with cheap power and cheap water.

110
00:06:07,892 --> 00:06:11,251
Its factories also faced looser pollution rules.

111
00:06:11,251 --> 00:06:17,877
And then cheap Chinese penicillin flooded the world market... at prices nobody else could match.

112
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:19,745
Now remember this one number.

113
00:06:19,745 --> 00:06:23,528
Nineteen ninety-one — the year India opened up its economy.

114
00:06:23,528 --> 00:06:29,490
Of all the medicine powder India bought from outside, China sold less than one per cent.

115
00:06:29,490 --> 00:06:31,059
Less than one.

116
00:06:31,059 --> 00:06:35,578
Then, one by one, the Indian penicillin plants went quiet.

117
00:06:35,578 --> 00:06:37,211
Hindustan Antibiotics.

118
00:06:37,211 --> 00:06:38,117
Stopped.

119
00:06:38,117 --> 00:06:39,126
I.D.P.L.

120
00:06:39,126 --> 00:06:40,047
Stopped.

121
00:06:40,047 --> 00:06:40,873
Torrent.

122
00:06:40,873 --> 00:06:41,891
Ranbaxy.

123
00:06:41,891 --> 00:06:42,840
Sarabhai.

124
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:43,714
Stopped.

125
00:06:43,714 --> 00:06:45,332
And the last one standing...

126
00:06:45,332 --> 00:06:46,274
Alembic.

127
00:06:46,274 --> 00:06:47,265
Stopped.

128
00:06:47,265 --> 00:06:52,579
By about twenty twenty, India was importing all of that base powder for amoxicillin.

129
00:06:52,579 --> 00:06:54,340
Every last kilo.

130
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:55,946
Remember that one per cent?

131
00:06:55,946 --> 00:06:58,176
That was for all medicine powder.

132
00:06:58,176 --> 00:07:01,588
Now, if you look at just antibiotic powder today...

133
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:04,587
China's share is around eighty-six per cent.

134
00:07:04,587 --> 00:07:11,134
Niti Aayog estimates Chinese powder costs thirty-five to forty per cent less than powder made in India.

135
00:07:11,134 --> 00:07:15,126
So tell me — if you ran a company, would you build a plant here?

136
00:07:15,126 --> 00:07:16,223
That's the trap.

137
00:07:16,223 --> 00:07:18,550
You can't compete without a big plant.

138
00:07:18,550 --> 00:07:22,889
And you can't risk a big plant... when one price war can wipe it out.

139
00:07:22,889 --> 00:07:24,980
For years, that trap held.

140
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:28,834
Then Corona came — and India had to lock its own doors.

141
00:07:28,834 --> 00:07:32,418
And this time, the central government decided to break the trap.

142
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:39,314
It launched a scheme to pay companies extra for making forty-one of these missing ingredients in India.

143
00:07:39,314 --> 00:07:42,928
Nearly seven thousand crore rupees, set aside.

144
00:07:42,928 --> 00:07:46,205
And one company took the biggest bet of all.

145
00:07:46,205 --> 00:07:48,349
Kakinada, Andhra Pradesh.

146
00:07:48,349 --> 00:07:54,596
On the coast, a new plant goes up, built by Aurobindo Pharma, through its unit called Lyfius.

147
00:07:54,596 --> 00:07:57,715
Inside are the giant tanks I just told you about.

148
00:07:57,715 --> 00:08:06,694
The company says it cost around two thousand five hundred crore rupees, and it's built to make fifteen thousand tonnes of penicillin G every year.

149
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:09,977
In twenty twenty-four, the tanks start running.

150
00:08:09,977 --> 00:08:12,850
For the first time in more than ten years...

151
00:08:12,850 --> 00:08:16,160
India is growing its own penicillin again.

152
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,910
But you know the trap.

153
00:08:17,910 --> 00:08:22,916
Even with Indian penicillin ready, cheap imports were still waiting at the port.

154
00:08:22,916 --> 00:08:27,414
So on the twenty-ninth of January, twenty twenty-six, the government stepped in.

155
00:08:27,414 --> 00:08:29,850
It set a minimum price at the border.

156
00:08:29,850 --> 00:08:36,833
If penicillin powder comes in cheaper than about two thousand two hundred rupees a kilo, it now needs a special licence.

157
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:40,151
The same rule covers amoxicillin and its base powder.

158
00:08:40,151 --> 00:08:41,858
Think of it as a shield.

159
00:08:41,858 --> 00:08:46,786
It gives the new Indian plant breathing room, while it grows big enough to stand on its own.

160
00:08:46,786 --> 00:08:56,801
And in September twenty twenty-six, after the Kakinada plant complained, the government also started checking whether China is selling penicillin here below a fair price.

161
00:08:56,801 --> 00:08:59,487
But that shield has an end date.

162
00:08:59,487 --> 00:09:04,099
It runs for one year... until January twenty twenty-seven.

163
00:09:04,099 --> 00:09:05,784
That's the date to watch.

164
00:09:05,784 --> 00:09:08,184
Will Kakinada be strong enough by then?

165
00:09:08,184 --> 00:09:10,417
Or will the shield get extended?

166
00:09:10,417 --> 00:09:13,260
And here's the balance the government has to strike.

167
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:17,611
Protect the Indian plant... without making your antibiotics costlier.

168
00:09:17,611 --> 00:09:19,253
And it's not just penicillin.

169
00:09:19,253 --> 00:09:23,834
Companies have already put more than five thousand crore rupees into this scheme.

170
00:09:23,834 --> 00:09:25,248
And there's more coming.

171
00:09:25,248 --> 00:09:32,369
Three giant bulk drug parks are being built — in Gujarat, in Himachal Pradesh... and one at Nakkapalli.

172
00:09:32,369 --> 00:09:38,218
Yes, you heard right — that's in Andhra Pradesh too, the same state as the Kakinada plant.

173
00:09:38,218 --> 00:09:39,660
Let me be honest with you.

174
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:42,054
None of those parks is up and running yet.

175
00:09:42,054 --> 00:09:47,185
And China has a thirty-year head start, and makes far more penicillin than we do.

176
00:09:47,185 --> 00:09:48,972
So has India won?

177
00:09:48,972 --> 00:09:49,850
Not yet.

178
00:09:49,850 --> 00:09:51,748
But it's back in the fight.

179
00:09:51,748 --> 00:09:53,032
So here's the lesson.

180
00:09:53,032 --> 00:09:58,989
If you only master the last step, you're only as strong as whoever controls the step before.

181
00:09:58,989 --> 00:10:00,001
And the cost?

182
00:10:00,001 --> 00:10:01,691
You saw it in the Corona days.

183
00:10:01,691 --> 00:10:07,097
When one province in China shut down, the pharmacy of the world had to lock its own doors.

184
00:10:07,097 --> 00:10:08,873
But here's the reality today.

185
00:10:08,873 --> 00:10:10,659
India has the scientists.

186
00:10:10,659 --> 00:10:12,259
It has the factories.

187
00:10:12,259 --> 00:10:15,505
And now, it's growing its own penicillin again.

188
00:10:15,505 --> 00:10:17,270
So what does this mean for you?

189
00:10:17,270 --> 00:10:20,483
Keep taking your medicines exactly as your doctor says.

190
00:10:20,483 --> 00:10:22,620
Nothing in this story changes that.

191
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:26,589
But the next time you take an antibiotic, think about that white powder.

192
00:10:26,589 --> 00:10:30,109
There's a fair chance part of its journey began in China.

193
00:10:30,109 --> 00:10:35,966
And if the plant in Kakinada wins... the next one might start right here in India.

194
00:10:35,966 --> 00:10:38,714
Medicines aren't the only missing piece.

195
00:10:38,714 --> 00:10:41,318
India writes software for the whole world.

196
00:10:41,318 --> 00:10:46,597
So why is India's own A.I. still so far behind America's and China's?

197
00:10:46,597 --> 00:10:48,200
That's our next story.

198
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:54,977
Before you go, tell me in the comments — which medicine in your home would you most like to see fully made in India?

199
00:10:54,977 --> 00:10:56,593
I read every one.

200
00:10:56,593 --> 00:10:58,598
This is Be Practical with Kishore.

201
00:10:58,598 --> 00:10:59,763
Stay practical.

202
00:10:59,763 --> 00:11:00,443
Jai Hind.

